    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0323" n="313" xml:id="pg313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-07T14:00:00-05:00">October 7, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>642. Reference Department’s 633, October 2, 9 p.m., also Saigon’s 102, October 1,
                    8 a.m.,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d327-f1"/> and Hanoi’s 149, October 3, 5 p.m.,
                    which have been repeated to you, Japanese actions in Indochina.</p>
                <p>If you have not already taken up this matter with the Foreign Minister the
                    Department suggests that you do so at the first opportunity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d327-f1" n="3" xml:id="d327-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 102 not printed.</p>
            </note>
